{
  "info": {
    "name": "Prestamaz - API de contactados",
    "description": "Consulta a quien contacto Prestamaz en una fecha o rango.\n\nANTES DE EMPEZAR:\n1. Abre la pestana 'Variables' de esta coleccion.\n2. Pon tu llave en `api_key` (Prestamaz te la entrega por separado).\n3. En `fecha_con_datos` pon un dia en el que sepas que hubo envios.\n   IMPORTANTE: llena la columna CURRENT VALUE, no solo INITIAL VALUE - Postman manda\n   la primera. Si la dejas vacia, las peticiones fallaran con error de formato.\n\nLuego corre la coleccion completa (Run collection). Las cuatro primeras deben responder\n200; las cinco de la carpeta 'Errores' deben fallar A PROPOSITO, y sus pruebas verifican\njusto eso. Todas las pruebas en verde = el API funciona.\n\nLas peticiones de la carpeta 'Errores' NO usan variables: llevan fechas fijas para que\ndemuestren el error que les toca aunque no hayas configurado nada.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://sender.prestamaz.site",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "api_key",
      "value": "PEGA_AQUI_TU_LLAVE",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "fecha_con_datos",
      "value": "2026-08-24",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "fecha_inicio",
      "value": "2026-08-01",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "fecha_fin",
      "value": "2026-08-31",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "apikey",
    "apikey": [
      {
        "key": "key",
        "value": "X-API-Key",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "value",
        "value": "{{api_key}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "in",
        "value": "header",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Un solo dia",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?date={{fecha_con_datos}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "contacted"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "date",
              "value": "{{fecha_con_datos}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Devuelve a quien se contacto ese dia.\n\nCada contacto sale UNA vez, aunque haya recibido varios mensajes. Las fechas son dias naturales en hora de Mexico: un mensaje de las 23:30 del 17 pertenece al 17."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('El status es ok', () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('ok'));",
              "pm.test('Trae data y meta', () => { pm.expect(j).to.have.property('data'); pm.expect(j).to.have.property('meta'); });",
              "pm.test('Cada fila trae name y phone', () => {",
              "  if (j.data.length) { pm.expect(j.data[0]).to.have.property('name'); pm.expect(j.data[0]).to.have.property('phone'); }",
              "});",
              "pm.test('No hay telefonos repetidos', () => {",
              "  const t = j.data.map(x => x.phone);",
              "  pm.expect(new Set(t).size).to.eql(t.length);",
              "});",
              "console.log('Contactados ese dia:', j.meta.total);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Un rango de fechas",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?from={{fecha_inicio}}&to={{fecha_fin}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "contacted"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "from",
              "value": "{{fecha_inicio}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "to",
              "value": "{{fecha_fin}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Las dos fechas se incluyen. Un contacto alcanzado varios dias del rango sale una sola vez."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('El rango se respeta', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(j.meta.from).to.eql(pm.variables.get('fecha_inicio'));",
              "  pm.expect(j.meta.to).to.eql(pm.variables.get('fecha_fin'));",
              "});",
              "console.log('Contactados en el rango:', j.meta.total);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Paginado - pagina 1",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?date={{fecha_con_datos}}&per_page=50&page=1",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "contacted"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "date",
              "value": "{{fecha_con_datos}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "per_page",
              "value": "50"
            },
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "1"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Por default trae 1,000 por pagina, maximo 5,000.\n\n`meta.pages` dice cuantas paginas hay: recorrelas hasta llegar a ese numero."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('Respeta el tamano de pagina', () => pm.expect(j.data.length).to.be.at.most(50));",
              "pm.test('Dice cuantas paginas hay', () => pm.expect(j.meta).to.have.property('pages'));",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('primera_pagina', JSON.stringify(j.data.map(x => x.phone)));",
              "console.log('Paginas totales:', j.meta.pages);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Paginado - pagina 2 (no debe repetir)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?date={{fecha_con_datos}}&per_page=50&page=2",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "contacted"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "date",
              "value": "{{fecha_con_datos}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "per_page",
              "value": "50"
            },
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "2"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Correla DESPUES de la pagina 1: la prueba compara las dos y verifica que ningun contacto se repita entre paginas."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Responde 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "const previa = pm.collectionVariables.get('primera_pagina');",
              "if (previa) {",
              "  const p1 = new Set(JSON.parse(previa));",
              "  const repetidos = j.data.filter(x => p1.has(x.phone));",
              "  pm.test('La pagina 2 no repite contactos de la 1', () => pm.expect(repetidos.length).to.eql(0));",
              "} else {",
              "  console.log('Corre primero la peticion 3 para poder comparar.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Errores",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sin llave - debe dar 401",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?date=2026-08-24",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "contacted"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "date",
                  "value": "2026-08-24"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sin la cabecera X-API-Key no se devuelve nada."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('Formato de error consistente', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('status', 'error');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('code');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Fecha mal escrita - debe dar INVALID_PARAMS",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?date=24/08/2026",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "contacted"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "date",
                  "value": "24/08/2026"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "El formato es AAAA-MM-DD. Cualquier otro se rechaza con un mensaje que dice como escribirla."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('El codigo es INVALID_PARAMS', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('INVALID_PARAMS'));",
                  "pm.test('El mensaje dice como escribirla', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('AAAA-MM-DD'));",
                  "pm.test('Formato de error consistente', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('status', 'error');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('code');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sin fecha - debe dar MISSING_DATE",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "contacted"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Hay que mandar `date`, o bien `from` y `to`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('El codigo es MISSING_DATE', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('MISSING_DATE'));",
                  "pm.test('Formato de error consistente', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('status', 'error');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('code');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Fecha y rango juntos - debe dar AMBIGUOUS_RANGE",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?date=2026-08-24&from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "contacted"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "date",
                  "value": "2026-08-24"
                },
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-08-01"
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-08-31"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "O una fecha, o un rango. Mandando las dos cosas no se sabe cual se quiso."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('El codigo es AMBIGUOUS_RANGE', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('AMBIGUOUS_RANGE'));",
                  "pm.test('Formato de error consistente', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('status', 'error');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('code');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Rango al reves - debe dar INVALID_RANGE",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/contacted?from=2026-08-31&to=2026-08-01",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "contacted"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "from",
                  "value": "2026-08-31"
                },
                {
                  "key": "to",
                  "value": "2026-08-01"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "La fecha final no puede ser anterior a la inicial."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Responde 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "pm.test('El codigo es INVALID_RANGE', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('INVALID_RANGE'));",
                  "pm.test('Formato de error consistente', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('status', 'error');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('message');",
                  "  pm.expect(j).to.have.property('code');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}